{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-94x4-5g3f-jjxp","published":"2026-10-09T15:31:33Z","modified":"2026-10-27T15:47:24.311989323Z","withdrawn":"2026-10-27T15:33:17Z","summary":"Duplicate Advisory: snappy-java: Unbounded memory allocation from attacker-declared uncompressed lengtha","details":"## Duplicate Advisory\n\nThis advisory has been withdrawn because it is a duplicate of GHSA-q233-g92q-qxp6. This link is maintained to preserve external references.\n\n## Original Description\nXerial snappy-java before 1.1.10.9 contains an unbounded memory allocation vulnerability that allows attackers to exhaust JVM memory by declaring a large uncompressed length in compressed input. Attackers can supply a few crafted bytes to Snappy.uncompress, uncompressString, SnappyInputStream or SnappyFramedInputStream to force allocations up to 2 GB, causing OutOfMemoryError and denial of service.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"org.xerial.snappy:snappy-java","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.xerial.snappy/snappy-java"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"}]}],"versions":["1.0.1-rc1","1.0.1-rc2","1.0.1-rc3","1.0.1-rc4","1.0.3","1.0.3-rc1","1.0.3-rc2","1.0.3-rc3","1.0.3-rc4","1.0.3.1","1.0.3.2","1.0.3.3","1.0.4","1.0.4.1","1.0.5","1.0.5-M1","1.0.5-M2","1.0.5-M3","1.0.5-M4","1.0.5.1","1.0.5.2","1.0.5.3","1.0.5.4","1.1.0","1.1.0-M1","1.1.0-M2","1.1.0-M3","1.1.0-M4","1.1.0.1","1.1.1","1.1.1-M1","1.1.1-M2","1.1.1-M3","1.1.1-M4","1.1.1.1","1.1.1.2","1.1.1.3","1.1.1.4","1.1.1.5","1.1.1.6","1.1.1.7","1.1.10.0","1.1.10.1","1.1.10.10","1.1.10.11","1.1.10.12","1.1.10.2","1.1.10.3","1.1.10.4","1.1.10.5","1.1.10.6","1.1.10.7","1.1.10.8","1.1.10.9","1.1.2","1.1.2-M1","1.1.2-RC1","1.1.2-RC2","1.1.2-RC3","1.1.2.1","1.1.2.2","1.1.2.3","1.1.2.4","1.1.2.5","1.1.2.6","1.1.3-M1","1.1.3-M2","1.1.4","1.1.4-M1","1.1.4-M2","1.1.4-M3","1.1.7","1.1.7.1","1.1.7.2","1.1.7.3","1.1.7.4","1.1.7.5","1.1.7.6","1.1.7.7","1.1.7.8","1.1.8","1.1.8.1","1.1.8.2","1.1.8.3","1.1.8.4","1.1.9.0","1.1